CTranslate2 (arlo-phoenix/CTranslate2-rocm) gfx803: cap the MIOpen Conv1D
workspace and survive its allocation failing.

Why: miopenConvolutionForwardGetWorkSpaceSize reports the worst case across
every solver MIOpen knows, including an im2col/GEMM fallback that asks for
~1.44GB on Whisper's first encoder conv (batch 1, 80ch x 3000 -> 768ch, k=3).
On gfx803 every solver the subsequent miopenFindConvolutionForwardAlgorithm
actually considers reports "no workspace required" (verified via
MIOPEN_LOG_LEVEL=6 on an RX 470: winograd/direct/naive all applicable with
zero workspace, only the never-chosen GEMM fallback drives the size), so the
huge allocation buys nothing - and when VRAM is short it fails, which
CTranslate2 surfaces as "CUDA failed with error out of memory" and the whole
transcription dies. That is the spurious-OOM failure mode documented in the
plugin repo's docs/ARCH_NOTES.md ("bogus OOM").

What: treat the reported size as a hint - cap it at 256MB, and if even the
capped allocation fails fall back to running the find with no workspace at
all, which restricts it to zero-workspace solvers instead of failing the
transcribe.

Applies to: arlo-phoenix/CTranslate2-rocm @ rocm branch (the fork is
unmaintained, so this is carried here rather than upstreamed). Applied by
docker/Dockerfile's ct2-source stage for ROCM_ARCH=gfx803 only.

diff --git a/src/ops/conv1d_gpu.cu b/src/ops/conv1d_gpu.cu
index e7006e4..c94e3f2 100644
--- a/src/ops/conv1d_gpu.cu
+++ b/src/ops/conv1d_gpu.cu
@@ -74,10 +74,27 @@ namespace ctranslate2 {
                                                           &workspace_size));
       if(workspace_size <= 0)
         workspace_size = last_workspace_size;
+      // GetWorkSpaceSize reports the worst case across every solver MIOpen
+      // knows, including an im2col/GEMM fallback that asks for ~1.4GB on
+      // Whisper's first conv (1x80x3000 -> 768) - while every solver that is
+      // actually applicable on gfx803 needs no workspace at all, so the find
+      // below never uses that fallback. Treat the number as a hint rather
+      // than a requirement: cap it, and if even the capped allocation fails,
+      // run the find with no workspace, which restricts it to zero-workspace
+      // solvers instead of failing the whole transcription with a spurious
+      // "out of memory".
+      const size_t workspace_cap = 256ull * 1024 * 1024;
+      if (workspace_size > workspace_cap)
+        workspace_size = workspace_cap;
       if (workspace_size > 0)
       {
-        workspace = get_allocator<Device::CUDA>().allocate(workspace_size);
-        last_workspace_size = workspace_size;
+        try {
+          workspace = get_allocator<Device::CUDA>().allocate(workspace_size);
+          last_workspace_size = workspace_size;
+        } catch (...) {
+          workspace = nullptr;
+          workspace_size = 0;
+        }
       }
       {
       miopenConvAlgoPerf_t convForwardAlgos;
